  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Add a togglable option for avatar marketplace creators to allow model downloads for editing (Caveat being that they cannot upload their model to other marketplaces because it breaks this functionality). Upon getting the file the user will also have a token saved to their VRChat account for permission to upload the avatar.\n\nEvery avatar that has been uploaded to VRChat will go through screening, where a script will open and inspect the Unity file, take pictures of it and reverse match any marketplace creators who enabled this feature. If there is good amount of matches, a manual review will occur to either allow, or block the upload of the avatar to prevent excess pirating.\n\nThis can however lead to cat and mouse situation with pirating, which is less than ideal.\n\nThis isn't a one-size-fits-all solution, but this is the closest idea I've gotten to prevent excess pirating in VRChat for future creators.",
